#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasikal ke masalah quantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dataset preparation {#dataset-preparation}"
msgstr "Persiapan dataset {#dataset-preparation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we use a real-world biological dataset for a binary classification task, which is generated by Daniels et al. (2022) and can be downloaded from the  [supplementary material](https://www.science.org/doi/full/10.1126/science.abq0225#supplementary-materials) included with the paper. The data consists of CAR T-cells, which are genetically engineered T-cells used in immunotherapy to treat certain cancers. T-cells, a type of immune cell, are modified in a lab to express chimeric antigen receptors (CARs) that target specific proteins on cancer cells. These modified T-cells can recognize and destroy cancer cells more effectively. The data features are the CAR T-cell motifs, which refer to the specific structural or functional component of the CAR engineered into T-cells. Based on these motifs, our task is to predict the cytotoxicity of a given CAR T-cell, labeling it as either toxic or non-toxic.\n"
"The following shows the helper functions to preprocess this dataset.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam tutorial ini kita menggunakan dataset biologis dunia nyata untuk tugas klasifikasi biner, yang dihasilkan oleh Daniels et al. (2022) dan dapat diunduh dari [supplementary material](https://www.science.org/doi/full/10.1126/science.abq0225#supplementary-materials) yang disertakan dalam makalah tersebut. Data terdiri dari CAR T-cell, yaitu sel T yang direkayasa secara genetik untuk digunakan dalam imunoterapi guna mengobati kanker tertentu. Sel T, sejenis sel imun, dimodifikasi di laboratorium untuk mengekspresikan chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) yang menargetkan protein spesifik pada sel kanker. Sel T yang telah dimodifikasi ini dapat mengenali dan menghancurkan sel kanker dengan lebih efektif. Fitur data adalah motif CAR T-cell, yang merujuk pada komponen struktural atau fungsional spesifik dari CAR yang direkayasa ke dalam sel T. Berdasarkan motif-motif ini, tugas kita adalah memprediksi sitotoksisitas dari suatu CAR T-cell, melabelinya sebagai toksik atau tidak toksik.\n"
"Berikut adalah fungsi-fungsi helper untuk melakukan preprocessing dataset ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can run this tutorial by running the following cell, which automatically creates the required folder structure and downloads both the training and test files directly into your environment. If you already have these files locally, this step will safely overwrite them to ensure version consistency.\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa menjalankan tutorial ini dengan menjalankan sel berikut, yang secara otomatis membuat struktur folder yang diperlukan dan mengunduh file training dan test langsung ke lingkunganmu. Jika kamu sudah memiliki file-file ini secara lokal, langkah ini akan menimpanya untuk memastikan konsistensi versi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also transform the dataset such that $1$ is represented as $\\pi/2$ for scaling purposes.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga mentransformasi dataset sehingga $1$ direpresentasikan sebagai $\\pi/2$ untuk keperluan scaling.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We verify sizes and shapes of the training and test datasets.\n"
msgstr "Kita memverifikasi ukuran dan bentuk dari dataset training dan test.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi pada perangkat keras kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit {#quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Circuit kuantum {#quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now construct the feature map that embeds our classical dataset into a higher-dimensional feature space. For this embedding, we use the [``ZZFeatureMap``](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ZZFeatureMap) from Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita buat feature map yang memetakan dataset klasik kita ke ruang fitur berdimensi lebih tinggi. Untuk embedding ini, kita pakai [`ZZFeatureMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ZZFeatureMap) dari Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/projected-quantum-kernels/extracted-outputs/45956df4-5472-4394-a3e1-5514c456791d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/projected-quantum-kernels/extracted-outputs/45956df4-5472-4394-a3e1-5514c456791d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another quantum embedding option is the 1D-Heisenberg Hamiltonian evolution ansatz. You can skip running this section if you would like to continue with the `ZZFeatureMap`.\n"
msgstr "Pilihan embedding kuantum lain adalah ansatz evolusi Hamiltonian 1D-Heisenberg. Kamu bisa lewati bagian ini kalau mau langsung lanjut dengan `ZZFeatureMap`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/projected-quantum-kernels/extracted-outputs/659dbf23-fd3f-4e01-94b4-33e6d672172c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/projected-quantum-kernels/extracted-outputs/659dbf23-fd3f-4e01-94b4-33e6d672172c-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure 1-RDMs {#measure-1-rdms}"
msgstr "Ukur 1-RDM {#measure-1-rdms}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this step, we obtain all single-qubit reduced density matrices (1-RDMs) through projective measurements of the quantum feature map, which will later be provided into the classical exponential kernel function.\n"
"Let's look at how to compute the 1-RDM given a single data point from the dataset before we run over all data. The 1-RDMs are a collection of single-qubit measurements of Pauli ``X``, ``Y`` and ``Z`` operators on all qubits. This is because a single-qubit RDM can be fully expressed as: $$\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\big( I + \\braket \\sigma_x \\sigma_x  + \\braket \\sigma_y \\sigma_y + \\braket \\sigma_z \\sigma_z  \\big)$$\n"
"First we select the backend to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di langkah ini, kita dapatkan semua single-qubit reduced density matrices (1-RDM) melalui pengukuran projektif dari feature map kuantum, yang nantinya akan dimasukkan ke fungsi kernel eksponensial klasik.\n"
"Mari kita lihat cara menghitung 1-RDM untuk satu data point dari dataset sebelum kita jalankan untuk semua data. 1-RDM adalah kumpulan pengukuran single-qubit operator Pauli `X`, `Y` dan `Z` pada semua qubit. Ini karena single-qubit RDM bisa dinyatakan sepenuhnya sebagai: $$\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\big( I + \\braket \\sigma_x \\sigma_x  + \\braket \\sigma_y \\sigma_y + \\braket \\sigma_z \\sigma_z  \\big)$$\n"
"Pertama kita pilih backend yang akan digunakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then we run the quantum circuit and measure the projections. Note that we turn on error mitigation, including Zero Noise Extrapolation (ZNE).\n"
msgstr "Kemudian kita jalankan Circuit kuantum dan ukur proyeksinya. Perhatikan bahwa kita mengaktifkan error mitigation, termasuk Zero Noise Extrapolation (ZNE).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next we retrieve the results.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya kita ambil hasilnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We print out the circuit size and the two-qubit gate depth.\n"
msgstr "Kita cetak ukuran Circuit dan kedalaman gate dua-qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/projected-quantum-kernels/extracted-outputs/4f573436-ec5c-451b-976c-ad718b3c201d-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/projected-quantum-kernels/extracted-outputs/4f573436-ec5c-451b-976c-ad718b3c201d-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now loop over the entire training dataset to obtain all 1-RDMs.\n"
"We also provide the results from an experiment that we ran on quantum hardware. You can either run the training yourself by setting the flag below to `True`, or use the projection results that we provide.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang bisa iterasi seluruh dataset pelatihan untuk mendapatkan semua 1-RDM.\n"
"Kita juga menyediakan hasil dari eksperimen yang sudah kita jalankan pada perangkat keras kuantum. Kamu bisa menjalankan pelatihan sendiri dengan mengatur flag di bawah ke `True`, atau pakai hasil proyeksi yang sudah kita sediakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once the jobs are complete, we can retrieve the results.\n"
msgstr "Setelah semua job selesai, kita bisa ambil hasilnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We repeat this for the test set.\n"
msgstr "Kita ulangi ini untuk test set.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can retrieve the results as before.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa ambil hasilnya seperti sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the projected quantum kernel {#define-the-projected-quantum-kernel}"
msgstr "Definisikan projected quantum kernel {#define-the-projected-quantum-kernel}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The projected quantum kernel is defined with the following kernel function: $$k^{\\textrm{PQ}}(x_i, x_j) = \\textrm{exp} \\Big(-\\gamma \\sum_k \\sum_{P \\in \\{ X,Y,Z \\}} (\\textrm{Tr}[P \\rho_k(x_i)] - \\textrm{Tr}[P \\rho_k(x_j)])^2 \\Big) $$\n"
"In the above equation, $\\gamma>0$ is a tunable hyperparameter. The $K^{\\textrm{PQ}}_{ij} = k^{\\textrm{PQ}}(x_i, x_j)$ are the entries of the kernel matrix $K^{\\textrm{PQ}}$.\n"
"Using the definition of 1-RDMs, we can see that the individual terms within the kernel function can be evaluated as $\\textrm{Tr}[P \\rho_k (x_i)] = \\braket P$, where $P \\in \\{ X,Y,Z \\}$. These expectation values are precisely what we measured above.\n"
"By using ``scikit-learn``, we can in fact compute the kernel even more easily. This is due to the readily available radial basis function (``'rbf'``) kernel: $ \\textrm{exp} (-\\gamma \\lVert x - x' \\rVert^2)$. First, we simply need to reshape the new projected training and test datasets into two-dimensional arrays.\n"
"Note that going over the entire dataset can take about 80 minutes on the QPU. To make sure that the rest of the tutorial is easily executable, we additionally provide projections from a previously run experiment (which are included in the files you downloaded in the `Download dataset` code block). If you performed the training yourself, you can continue the tutorial with your own results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Projected quantum kernel didefinisikan dengan fungsi kernel berikut: $$k^{\\textrm{PQ}}(x_i, x_j) = \\textrm{exp} \\Big(-\\gamma \\sum_k \\sum_{P \\in \\{ X,Y,Z \\}} (\\textrm{Tr}[P \\rho_k(x_i)] - \\textrm{Tr}[P \\rho_k(x_j)])^2 \\Big) $$\n"
"Pada persamaan di atas, $\\gamma>0$ adalah hyperparameter yang bisa disetel. $K^{\\textrm{PQ}}_{ij} = k^{\\textrm{PQ}}(x_i, x_j)$ adalah entri dari matriks kernel $K^{\\textrm{PQ}}$.\n"
"Dengan menggunakan definisi 1-RDM, kita bisa lihat bahwa setiap suku dalam fungsi kernel dapat dievaluasi sebagai $\\textrm{Tr}[P \\rho_k (x_i)] = \\braket P$, di mana $P \\in \\{ X,Y,Z \\}$. Nilai ekspektasi ini persis seperti yang kita ukur di atas.\n"
"Dengan menggunakan ``scikit-learn``, kita sebenarnya bisa menghitung kernel dengan lebih mudah. Ini karena tersedianya kernel radial basis function (``'rbf'``) yang siap pakai: $ \\textrm{exp} (-\\gamma \\lVert x - x' \\rVert^2)$. Pertama, kita cukup mengubah bentuk dataset training dan test yang sudah diproyeksikan menjadi array dua dimensi.\n"
"Perlu diperhatikan bahwa memproses seluruh dataset bisa memakan waktu sekitar 80 menit di QPU. Untuk memastikan sisa tutorial ini mudah dijalankan, kita juga menyediakan proyeksi dari eksperimen yang sudah pernah dijalankan sebelumnya (yang disertakan dalam file yang kamu unduh di blok kode `Download dataset`). Jika kamu sudah melakukan training sendiri, kamu bisa melanjutkan tutorial dengan hasilmu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support Vector Machine (SVM) {#support-vector-machine-svm}"
msgstr "Support Vector Machine (SVM) {#support-vector-machine-svm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run a classical SVM on this precomputed kernel, and use the kernel between test and training sets for prediction.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita bisa menjalankan SVM klasik pada kernel yang sudah dihitung sebelumnya, dan menggunakan kernel antara set test dan training untuk prediksi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical benchmarking {#classical-benchmarking}"
msgstr "Benchmarking klasik {#classical-benchmarking}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can run a classical SVM with the radial basis function as the kernel without doing a quantum projection. This result is our classical benchmark.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menjalankan SVM klasik dengan radial basis function sebagai kernel tanpa melakukan proyeksi kuantum. Hasil ini adalah tolok ukur klasik kita.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix: Verify the dataset's potential quantum advantage in learning tasks {#appendix-verify-the-datasets-potential-quantum-advantage-in-learning-tasks}"
msgstr "Lampiran: Verifikasi potensi keunggulan kuantum dataset dalam tugas pembelajaran {#appendix-verify-the-datasets-potential-quantum-advantage-in-learning-tasks}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not all datasets offer potential advantage from the use of PQKs. There are some theoretical bounds that one can use as a preliminary test to see if a particular dataset can benefit from PQKs. To quantify this, authors of [Power of data in quantum machine learning](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-22539-9) [2] define quantities referred to as classical and quantum model complexities and geometric separation of the classical and quantum models. To expect a potential quantum advantage from PQKs, the geometric separation between the classical and quantum-projected kernels should be approximately on the order of $\\sqrt{N}$, where $N$ is the number of training samples. If this condition is satisfied, we move on to checking the model complexities. If the classical model complexity is on the order of $N$ while the quantum-projected model complexity is substantially smaller than $N$, we can expect potential advantage from the PQK.\n"
"Geometric separation is defined as follows (F19 in [[2]](#references)):\n"
"$$g_{cq} = g(K^c \\Vert K^q) = \\sqrt{\\Vert \\sqrt{K^q} \\sqrt{K^c} (K^c + \\lambda I)^{-2} \\sqrt{K^c} \\sqrt{K^q}\\Vert_{\\infty}}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak semua dataset menawarkan potensi keunggulan dari penggunaan PQK. Ada beberapa batas teoritis yang bisa digunakan sebagai uji awal untuk melihat apakah dataset tertentu bisa mendapat manfaat dari PQK. Untuk mengukur ini, para penulis [Power of data in quantum machine learning](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-22539-9) [2] mendefinisikan besaran yang disebut kompleksitas model klasik dan kuantum serta pemisahan geometris dari model klasik dan kuantum. Untuk mengharapkan potensi keunggulan kuantum dari PQK, pemisahan geometris antara kernel klasik dan kernel yang diproyeksikan secara kuantum harus kira-kira dalam orde $\\sqrt{N}$, di mana $N$ adalah jumlah sampel training. Jika kondisi ini terpenuhi, kita lanjut memeriksa kompleksitas model. Jika kompleksitas model klasik dalam orde $N$ sementara kompleksitas model yang diproyeksikan secara kuantum jauh lebih kecil dari $N$, kita bisa mengharapkan potensi keunggulan dari PQK.\n"
"Pemisahan geometris didefinisikan sebagai berikut (F19 dalam [[2]](#references)):\n"
"$$g_{cq} = g(K^c \\Vert K^q) = \\sqrt{\\Vert \\sqrt{K^q} \\sqrt{K^c} (K^c + \\lambda I)^{-2} \\sqrt{K^c} \\sqrt{K^q}\\Vert_{\\infty}}$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Model complexity is defined as follows (M1 in [[2]](#references)):\n"
"$$ s_{K, \\lambda}(N) = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\lambda^2 \\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=1}^N (K+\\lambda I)^{-2}_{ij} y_i y_j}{N}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=1}^N ((K+\\lambda I)^{-1}K(K+\\lambda I)^{-1})_{ij} y_i y_j}{N}}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kompleksitas model didefinisikan sebagai berikut (M1 dalam [[2]](#references)):\n"
"$$ s_{K, \\lambda}(N) = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\lambda^2 \\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=1}^N (K+\\lambda I)^{-2}_{ij} y_i y_j}{N}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=1}^N ((K+\\lambda I)^{-1}K(K+\\lambda I)^{-1})_{ij} y_i y_j}{N}}$$\n"

